        "prompt_content": "# v8.7.1 claims review (parent narrative, second prepare)\n\nDate: 2026-09-15. Reviewer: parent agent (prepared the release lane).\nObserver: distinct read-only subagent (`v871-claims-review-2`), verdict PASS.\n\nThis is a fresh review: the first prepare's line could not resume after a\nreviewer-demanded code repair landed on top of it, so the line was\nrecovered (backup ref `backup-871-release-attempt1`, reset to pre-prepare,\ncontent replayed) and prepared anew. This narrative binds the NEW prepared\ncommit `34e767973e60fff9fcadf054e165085356e44f6b` only.\n\n## What was audited\n\nThe prepared record `charness-artifacts/release/latest.md` at `34e767973` —\nits assertions only, not code correctness (covered by the release critique\nworker and the standing suite).\n\n## Observer findings (all hold)\n\n1. Previous 8.7.0 in pre-bump manifests; target 8.7.1 on every versioned\n   surface (3 version lines in packaging, 2 in marketplace).\n2. Tag `v8.7.1` absent locally and on origin; latest published tag `v8.7.0`.\n3. Branch `main`, remote `origin`.\n4. No-drift report matches an independent `current_release.py` re-run\n   exactly (4 versioned + 1 presence-only).\n5. Fresh-checkout probe set matches the declared set.\n6. Critique artifact exists and is tracked.\n7. Bump rationale rendered verbatim.\n8. Quality numbers internally consistent (exit 0 in 163.0s vs 163.021s);\n   pending states honestly bounded; no overclaim.\n\n## Minor observations (not failures)\n\n- Probe-pass status rests on the helper's own probe runs (advisory).\n- Bare `current_release.py` re-run reports probes `not_established`\n  (expected; probes run under the helper, not the listing).\n\n## Out of scope (not counted against)\n\nCode correctness — owned by the critique artifact and the standing suite.\n\n## Disposition\n\nNo unsupported numbers, figures, or verification sentences found.\nProceed to resume publication.\n",
